      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The stereoselective synthesis of (E)-trisubstituted tertiary enamides is documented via site-selective Ni-catalyzed β-arylation of allenamides with boronic acids in high yields (up to 89%). The nucleophilic character of the \"organo-Ni\" intermediates is further exploited to implement a one-pot tricomponent procedure involving the final allylation of aldehydes (yields up to 93%). Mechanistic insights and efficiency on a gram scale process were also documented."},
